# Fork: findings the secret scan (.github/scripts/fork-secret-scan.sh) may skip, one per line, each
# with a comment saying what it is and why it is safe.
#
# Form: file:rule:line (no commit), for example
#   apps/server/src/example.test.ts:generic-api-key:12
# Such a line matches that finding in every commit, so it still matches after a squash merge gives
# the commit a new id. A line pinned to a commit (commit:file:rule:line) stops matching then, and the
# default branch's push scan fails on the same finding; the scan warns about such lines.
# Prefer a `gitleaks:allow` comment on the line itself where the file allows one.
#
# The scan reads this file from the default branch (a pull request) or the tip before the push, so a
# change here applies once it is merged: land it in a pull request of its own first.
